WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:02.334
-Good evening! I'm Seth Meyers.

00:00:02.334 --> 00:00:03.870
This is "Late Night."
We hope you're all doing well.

00:00:03.870 --> 00:00:05.038
And now, if you don't mind,
we're going to get to the news.

00:00:05.038 --> 00:00:07.207
The Colorado Supreme Court
ruled yesterday

00:00:07.207 --> 00:00:09.676
that former President Trump
is ineligible

00:00:09.676 --> 00:00:11.044
to run again for president,

00:00:11.044 --> 00:00:14.314
while the Florida Supreme Court
ruled he already won.

00:00:14.314 --> 00:00:17.016
[ Laughter ]

00:00:17.016 --> 00:00:19.785
Supreme Court Chief Justice
John Roberts spoke yesterday

00:00:19.785 --> 00:00:23.022
at the memorial service
for Justice Sandra Day O'Connor

00:00:23.022 --> 00:00:25.225
and said "she was so successful

00:00:25.225 --> 00:00:28.594
that the barriers she broke down
are almost unthinkable today,"

00:00:28.594 --> 00:00:30.497
adding,
"but we're working on it."

00:00:30.497 --> 00:00:31.831
[ Laughter ]

00:00:31.831 --> 00:00:33.799
At a rally last night in Iowa,

00:00:33.799 --> 00:00:36.168
former President Trump
told the crowd that immigrants

00:00:36.168 --> 00:00:38.337
are "destroying the blood
of our country."

00:00:38.337 --> 00:00:40.706
Pretty ironic thing
to say in a state

00:00:40.706 --> 00:00:43.142
that only exists
to produce corn syrup.

00:00:43.142 --> 00:00:45.979
[ Laughter ]

00:00:45.979 --> 00:00:48.314
After facing comparisons
to Adolf Hitler,

00:00:48.314 --> 00:00:49.949
former President Trump
said yesterday

00:00:49.949 --> 00:00:52.251
that immigrants are destroying
the blood of our country

00:00:52.251 --> 00:00:53.753
and added, "They said,

00:00:53.753 --> 00:00:56.522
'oh, Hitler said that
in a much different way,'"

00:00:56.522 --> 00:00:58.957
but you've already lost
the argument if you have to say,

00:00:58.957 --> 00:01:02.395
"Guys, I wasn't quoting Hitler.
I was paraphrasing him!"

00:01:02.395 --> 00:01:05.465
[ Laughter ]

00:01:05.465 --> 00:01:07.933
That's right. After facing
comparisons to Adolf Hitler,

00:01:07.933 --> 00:01:09.669
Trump said that immigrants
are destroying the blood

00:01:09.669 --> 00:01:12.572
of our country and added,
"I've never read 'Mein Kampf,'"

00:01:12.572 --> 00:01:16.309
yet no one thought you had.

00:01:16.309 --> 00:01:18.945
I'd be surprised if you read
"The Art of the Deal."

00:01:18.945 --> 00:01:21.013
[ Laughter ]

00:01:21.013 --> 00:01:22.715
At a conservative conference
yesterday,

00:01:22.715 --> 00:01:24.616
Republican Senator Ted Cruz
told the crowd

00:01:24.616 --> 00:01:26.386
that the left is unhappy
and added,

00:01:26.386 --> 00:01:28.053
"if you were a liberal woman

00:01:28.053 --> 00:01:29.822
and you had to sleep
with those weenies,

00:01:29.822 --> 00:01:30.923
you'd be pissed too."

00:01:30.923 --> 00:01:32.859
Well, joke's on you, Ted,

00:01:32.859 --> 00:01:35.194
because liberal women
sleep with each other...

00:01:35.194 --> 00:01:38.898
[ Laughter ]

00:01:38.898 --> 00:01:39.832
...dude.

00:01:39.832 --> 00:01:41.901
[ Laughter ]

00:01:41.901 --> 00:01:45.404
The scooter rental company Bird
has filed for bankruptcy.

00:01:45.404 --> 00:01:47.506
Apparently, it's not profitable
to charge people

00:01:47.506 --> 00:01:49.742
10 bucks to chuck
your scooters into the river.

00:01:49.742 --> 00:01:53.146
[ Laughter ]

00:01:53.146 --> 00:01:55.315
A 90-year-old woman
recently graduated

00:01:55.315 --> 00:01:58.217
from the University of North
Texas with a master's degree.

00:01:58.217 --> 00:02:00.186
At least I hope
that's what they meant

00:02:00.186 --> 00:02:01.520
when they said she passed.

00:02:01.520 --> 00:02:03.890
[ Audience groaning ]

00:02:10.262 --> 00:02:11.564
[ Mouthing silently ]

00:02:11.564 --> 00:02:12.832
[ Laughter ]

00:02:12.832 --> 00:02:15.334
Minnesota yesterday
unveiled its new state flag,

00:02:15.334 --> 00:02:17.236
which features
a light blue background

00:02:17.236 --> 00:02:18.638
with a white north star.

00:02:18.638 --> 00:02:21.307
The flag was designed
by Minnesota artist Lucas.

00:02:21.307 --> 00:02:25.511
[ Laughter ]

00:02:25.511 --> 00:02:28.314
Good. Lucas.

00:02:28.314 --> 00:02:31.117
A New Jersey police officer
was arrested yesterday

00:02:31.117 --> 00:02:33.753
for allegedly stealing drugs
from an evidence room.

00:02:33.753 --> 00:02:35.221
Police confiscated the drugs,

00:02:35.221 --> 00:02:37.423
but he's pretty sure
he knows how to get them back.

00:02:37.423 --> 00:02:39.859
[ Laughter ]

00:02:39.859 --> 00:02:41.827
Finally, the CDC estimated
this week

00:02:41.827 --> 00:02:44.631
that roughly 20% of
recent coronavirus infections

00:02:44.631 --> 00:02:47.600
have been caused by the newly
discovered subvariant JN.1,

00:02:47.600 --> 00:02:50.536
or as most Americans
are calling it, "allergies."

00:02:50.536 --> 00:02:52.438
And that was a monologue,
everybody!

00:02:52.438 --> 00:02:55.374
We are off and running.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:55.374 --> 00:02:57.810
We got a great show
for you tonight.

00:02:57.810 --> 00:03:00.279
You know him from
"Marriage Story," "Girls,"

00:03:00.279 --> 00:03:03.349
"House of Gucci," "Star Wars"
and as an excellent "SNL" host.

00:03:03.349 --> 00:03:06.185
His latest, "Ferrari,"
is in theaters on Christmas Day.

00:03:06.185 --> 00:03:07.987
Our friend Adam Driver is back.

00:03:07.987 --> 00:03:09.888
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:09.888 --> 00:03:12.625
We got Adam Driver
in the building.

00:03:12.625 --> 00:03:14.726
And he's
one of my favorite stand ups.

00:03:14.726 --> 00:03:17.163
His book, "Misfit: Growing Up
Awkward in the '80s,"

00:03:17.163 --> 00:03:19.766
is out now,
and his new stand up special,

00:03:19.766 --> 00:03:22.168
"Born on Third Base,"
premieres tomorrow on MAX.

00:03:22.168 --> 00:03:23.836
Gary Gulman
will be joining us.

00:03:23.836 --> 00:03:26.872
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:26.872 --> 00:03:30.275
Guys, I had a very --
I had a very big night

00:03:30.275 --> 00:03:31.477
personally last night.

00:03:31.477 --> 00:03:32.712
For the first time, I went --

00:03:32.712 --> 00:03:35.548
I saw Billy Joel in concert
at MSG.

00:03:35.548 --> 00:03:37.016
Oh, my goodness.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:37.016 --> 00:03:38.484
I'd heard great things,

00:03:38.484 --> 00:03:41.253
and one of the greatest concerts
I've ever been to.

00:03:41.253 --> 00:03:42.488
I would love to go again.
But guess what, guys.

00:03:42.488 --> 00:03:44.123
I don't need to go again

00:03:44.123 --> 00:03:45.491
'cause I took a cellphone video.

00:03:45.491 --> 00:03:47.827
[ Laughter ]

00:03:47.827 --> 00:03:50.095
Pretty smart.

00:03:50.095 --> 00:03:51.697
During "Piano Man,"
I think I was the only guy

00:03:51.697 --> 00:03:53.866
who thought about it.

00:03:53.866 --> 00:03:58.471
Took like a 45-second video
of the middle of "Piano Man."

00:03:58.471 --> 00:04:00.373
And now, I mean, I feel like
when people find out

00:04:00.373 --> 00:04:02.542
I have this...
bidding war.

00:04:02.542 --> 00:04:03.943
[ Laughter ]

00:04:03.943 --> 00:04:05.912
Can you imagine?

00:04:05.912 --> 00:04:08.514
45 seconds.

00:04:08.514 --> 00:04:12.017
Not even a full verse.
Just a weird middle.

00:04:12.017 --> 00:04:15.254
Weird in point.
Weird out point.

00:04:15.254 --> 00:04:17.189
Like, from
"real estate novelist"

00:04:17.189 --> 00:04:19.025
to "sing us" and then out.

00:04:19.025 --> 00:04:22.394
[ Laughter ]

00:04:22.394 --> 00:04:24.697
From so far away.

00:04:24.697 --> 00:04:26.966
From so far away,
that halfway through it,

00:04:26.966 --> 00:04:29.635
there's a weird zoom...

00:04:29.635 --> 00:04:32.305
that just, like,
really stretches the pixels.

00:04:34.073 --> 00:04:36.341
This video couldn't
exonerate Billy Joel

00:04:36.341 --> 00:04:38.578
if he was suspected of a crime.

00:04:38.578 --> 00:04:42.214
[ Laughter ]

00:04:42.214 --> 00:04:45.484
If the cops were like, "We like
Joel for the bank heist,"

00:04:45.484 --> 00:04:47.085
and I was like,
"It couldn't have been him.

00:04:47.085 --> 00:04:48.687
He was at
Madison Square Garden,"

00:04:48.687 --> 00:04:50.422
and showed it to them,

00:04:50.422 --> 00:04:52.925
they'd be like,
"Which one is he?"

00:04:52.925 --> 00:04:56.229
And I'd be like,
"The guy at the piano."

00:04:56.229 --> 00:04:59.665
And they'd say,
"What's the piano?"

00:04:59.665 --> 00:05:01.233
The best --
I had the best time.

00:05:01.233 --> 00:05:03.169
Scream singing.

00:05:03.169 --> 00:05:06.538
Scream singing
"We Didn't Start the Fire."

00:05:06.538 --> 00:05:08.441
Maybe got 10 words right.

00:05:08.441 --> 00:05:10.342
[ Laughter ]

00:05:10.342 --> 00:05:13.446
Confidently scr-- I said
"Bridge on the River Kwai"

00:05:13.446 --> 00:05:15.248
five times before I was right.

00:05:15.248 --> 00:05:17.183
[ Laughter ]

00:05:19.519 --> 00:05:22.154
Time of my life.

00:05:22.154 --> 00:05:24.289
So if you got a free night

00:05:24.289 --> 00:05:27.426
and you're in New York City,
go to Big Apple Circus.

00:05:27.426 --> 00:05:29.495
[ Laughter ]

00:05:29.495 --> 00:05:31.164
Look, you know,
Billy Joel is great.

00:05:31.164 --> 00:05:33.432
I don't have to sell Billy Joel.
He's a legend.

00:05:33.432 --> 00:05:35.868
I went to Big Apple Surface --
Circus. Excuse me.

00:05:35.868 --> 00:05:38.538
You guys, I've been
out and about this week.

00:05:38.538 --> 00:05:41.007
[ Laughter ]

00:05:41.007 --> 00:05:42.874
Big Apple Circus on Sunday.

00:05:42.874 --> 00:05:43.942
Billy Joel last night.

00:05:43.942 --> 00:05:46.913
I'm a man about town.

00:05:46.913 --> 00:05:49.449
Big Apple Circus is so good.

00:05:49.449 --> 00:05:51.483
At one point -- And, again,

00:05:51.483 --> 00:05:53.853
I am not connected to them
financially in any way.

00:05:53.853 --> 00:05:56.155
[ Laughter ]

00:05:56.155 --> 00:05:58.690
At one point,
a performer lies on their back

00:05:58.690 --> 00:06:00.359
and puts their feet up,
and they put --

00:06:00.359 --> 00:06:03.929
she has a table on her feet
and she just spins the table.

00:06:03.929 --> 00:06:06.432
And until that moment, I never
thought I wanted to see that.

00:06:06.432 --> 00:06:09.368
[ Laughter ]

00:06:09.368 --> 00:06:11.070
I never in my life
walked into a room,

00:06:11.070 --> 00:06:12.772
saw a table and was like,
"Oh, what I wouldn't give

00:06:12.772 --> 00:06:14.773
for someone to flip
that upside down

00:06:14.773 --> 00:06:16.908
and just like helicopter it."

00:06:16.908 --> 00:06:18.177
Kicks it up. Catch it.

00:06:18.177 --> 00:06:21.513
It was the greatest night
of my life.

00:06:21.513 --> 00:06:22.681
To quote Billy Joel...

00:06:22.681 --> 00:06:24.417
♪ Trouble in the Suez ♪

00:06:24.417 --> 00:06:26.685
[ Laughter ]

00:06:26.685 --> 00:06:31.657
You know, I talked a long time
about the circus on Monday...

00:06:31.657 --> 00:06:34.494
and then I read one of
the comments on YouTube.

00:06:34.494 --> 00:06:35.962
And you know what somebody said?

00:06:35.962 --> 00:06:39.098
"I guess a guest
must have dropped out."

00:06:39.098 --> 00:06:42.101
[ Laughter ]

00:06:46.105 --> 00:06:47.172
What's that?

00:06:47.172 --> 00:06:48.708
Oh, Adam Driver showed up?

00:06:48.708 --> 00:06:50.276
Okay, great.

00:06:50.276 --> 00:06:52.144
I can stop
with all this bull[bleep].

00:06:52.144 --> 00:06:53.946
[ Laughs ]

00:06:53.946 --> 00:06:56.615
You guys, moving on, Billy Joel!

00:06:56.615 --> 00:06:57.583
He's a legend. Moving on.

